  "summary": "A fast assault skirmisher behind a seamless shell. Four cycling emitters track well inside two hundred metres, then heat and distance take their price.",
  "lore": "The PLV stands just under the depot roof and was stored without a cradle, feet set directly in the floor. Its two paired emitter banks are sealed into the upper shell; there are no access plates and no alignment marks. Compact manuals describe a five-minute exchange of the complete upper hull. Tessell has no crane that can do it. An intact Pallvault crosses a firing lane before heavier machines have turned. A damaged one is a source of parts for the next.",
